    "sop": {
      "hook": "Being too sensitive might be a rare neurological gift.",
      "explain": "Scientists call it high sensory processing sensitivity. Your nervous system takes in more detail than most. You feel other people's moods like they're your own. The world hits you at a higher volume.",
      "reframe": "So being sensitive isn't weakness, it's a sharper antenna. You notice the things that make people feel seen. That depth is why people trust you with the real stuff. The same nerve that aches is the one that connects.",
      "cta_question": "Are you the sensitive one in your group, yes or no?",
      "specificity": "too sensitive"
    }
  }
